Package: sintHiChIP
Title: Accurate and Efficient HiChIP Interaction Detection by Modeling
    Restriction Enzyme Cut Site Density as Biological Signal
Version: 1.1.0
Authors@R: 
    person("Weiyue", "Ding", , "wyding0501@hotmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: sintHiChIP detects significant chromatin interactions in HiChIP data 
    by modeling restriction enzyme cut site density as biological signal. 
    Implements genome-wide bin-based analysis with adaptive statistical modeling 
    (binomial, negative binomial, or Poisson). Features HiC-Pro integration, 
    peak-to-peak and peak-to-non-peak interaction detection, numerical stability, 
    and WashU Browser track generation.
License: GPL-3 + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.0.0)
Imports: GenomeInfoDb, GenomicRanges, IRanges, Rcpp, S4Vectors,
        data.table, dplyr, matrixStats, methods, readr, stats, tools,
        graphics, MASS
SystemRequirements: bedtools (>= 2.29.0), tabix (>= 1.10), 
                    bgzip (>= 1.10), HiC-Pro (>= 3.1.0)
LinkingTo: Rcpp
RoxygenNote: 7.3.3
Suggests: testthat, knitr, rmarkdown
